 asset concept, then complete the linked mission task or AEGIS scenario response.","Mission Task Prompt":"Translate the source into a concrete mission decision, architecture judgment, or research gap statement.","Dash Deliverable":"Short written analysis with one visual and a reflective diary entry.","Evaluation Focus":"Systems thinking, mission relevance, trust-and-assurance reasoning, decision communication, and evidence quality."},"research":{"Source ID":"M11","Research Vector":"Design and test a multidisciplinary curriculum model for spacepower education aligned to emerging Guardian and civilian workforce needs.","Master''s-Level Option":"20-30 page applied research paper or design study linked to a weekly work plan and AEGIS scenario.","PhD / Publication Option":"Publication-oriented manuscript on the unresolved trust, assurance, architecture, or workforce issue surfaced by the source.","Cross-Links / Best-Fit Pathways":"Workforce & Education"}}'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do update set title=excluded.title, official_source=excluded.official_source, tier=excluded.tier, domain=excluded.domain, theme=excluded.theme, pathways=excluded.pathways, core_selective=excluded.core_selective, public_url=excluded.public_url, phase2=excluded.phase2, content=excluded.content, updated_at=now();
insert into public.sources (id,title,official_source,tier,domain,theme,pathways,core_selective,public_url,phase2,content) values ('M12','Objective Force 2040 Baseline','USSF','Tier 1 - Core Astrum Source','Force design / future','Investment signals, future force design, and strategic direction','Resilient Architectures; Mission Systems','Core','https://www.spaceforce.mil/News/Article-Display/Article/4421186/us-space-force-university-consortium-awards-new-tech-institutes-spotlights-majo/',false,'{"brief":{"Source ID":"M12","Brief ID":"AB-M12","Proposed Brief Title":"Objective Force 2040 Baseline","Brief Abstract / Teaching Angle":"This Astrum Brief contextualizes the source for mission-critical space education. It identifies why the material matters now, what it teaches about mission systems, and how it can be translated into an exercise, scenario, or research question rather than remaining a passive reading.","Key Learning Payoff":"Resilience, autonomy, machine-speed support, future operating environment.","What Changed / Why Now":"Force design is shifting toward proliferation, resilience, and reconstitution, which multiplies trust boundaries and cyber complexity.","Suggested Dash Deliverable":"Short written analysis with one visual and a reflective diary entry."},"lens":{"Source ID":"M12","Lens ID":"RL-M12","Raven''s Lens Commentary":"The Raven''s Lens uses the source to surface the trust assumptions hiding underneath the official language.","Hidden Assumption":"That the architecture will behave as designed even when the mission is stressed, degraded, or contested.","Likely Failure Point":"A mismatch between stated policy intent and the technical evidence available during real mission stress.","What They Didn''t Say":"How Astrum''s trust-and-assurance method should be applied to this exact mission problem.","Signature Raven Question":"What mission decision becomes dangerous if the assumptions in this source prove false?"},"questions":{"Source ID":"M12","CQ-1":"What