e judgment, or research gap statement.","Dash Deliverable":"Short written analysis with one visual and a reflective diary entry.","Evaluation Focus":"Systems thinking, mission relevance, trust-and-assurance reasoning, decision communication, and evidence quality."},"research":{"Source ID":"M12","Research Vector":"Identify a measurable trust, resilience, or mission-assurance gap implied by the source and frame it as a publishable research question.","Master''s-Level Option":"20-30 page applied research paper or design study linked to a weekly work plan and AEGIS scenario.","PhD / Publication Option":"Publication-oriented manuscript on the unresolved trust, assurance, architecture, or workforce issue surfaced by the source.","Cross-Links / Best-Fit Pathways":"Resilient Architectures; Mission Systems"}}'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do update set title=excluded.title, official_source=excluded.official_source, tier=excluded.tier, domain=excluded.domain, theme=excluded.theme, pathways=excluded.pathways, core_selective=excluded.core_selective, public_url=excluded.public_url, phase2=excluded.phase2, content=excluded.content, updated_at=now();
insert into public.sources (id,title,official_source,tier,domain,theme,pathways,core_selective,public_url,phase2,content) values ('M13','FY27 DAF Budget Testimony - Space Force Priorities','DAF/USSF','Tier 2 - Selective / elective source','Investment signals','Investment signals, future force design, and strategic direction','Acquisition & Strategy','Selective','https://www.spaceforce.mil/News/Article/2724710/ussf-und-sign-mou-establishing-university-partnership-program/',false,'{"brief":{"Source ID":"M13","Brief ID":"AB-M13","Proposed Brief Title":"FY27 DAF Budget Testimony - Space Force Priorities","Brief Abstract / Teaching Angle":"This brief treats the source as a strategic signal. Rather than merely summarizing a posture statement, assessment, or portfolio page, the brief identifies what it reveals about priorities, bottlenecks, investment logic, transition challenges, and the type of capabilities the U.S. national security space ecosystem is actually rewarding right now.","Key Learning Payoff":"Missile warning/tracking, SATCOM, space control, RDT&E.","What Changed / Why Now":"Astrum uses this source not as static reading, but as a current signal about how mission-critical space systems are being designed, governed, or stressed.","Suggested Dash Deliverable":"2-page memo or 6-slide commander brief uploaded in Dash."},"lens":{"Source ID":"M13","Lens ID":"RL-M13","Raven''s Lens Commentary":"Under the Raven''s Lens, these sources reveal the practical side of power: what gets funded, what gets delayed, what remains difficult to transition, and where rhetoric about capability still outruns institutional execution.","Hidden Assumption":"That the acquisition and oversight system can move at the speed of operational need.","Likely Failure Point":"Transition lag between promising ideas and fielded, supportable capability.","What They Didn''t Say":"Which educational, cultural, and contractual changes are needed for faster, more trustworthy fielding.","Signature Raven Que