ure judgment, or research gap statement.","Dash Deliverable":"2-page memo or 6-slide commander brief uploaded in Dash.","Evaluation Focus":"Systems thinking, mission relevance, trust-and-assurance reasoning, decision communication, and evidence quality."},"research":{"Source ID":"M35","Research Vector":"Research how doctrine and strategic guidance account for trusted data, cyber resilience, and commercial integration in actual decision chains.","Master''s-Level Option":"20-30 page applied research paper or design study linked to a weekly work plan and AEGIS scenario.","PhD / Publication Option":"Publication-oriented manuscript on the unresolved trust, assurance, architecture, or workforce issue surfaced by the source.","Cross-Links / Best-Fit Pathways":"Space Cybersecurity; Mission Assurance"}}'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do update set title=excluded.title, official_source=excluded.official_source, tier=excluded.tier, domain=excluded.domain, theme=excluded.theme, pathways=excluded.pathways, core_selective=excluded.core_selective, public_url=excluded.public_url, phase2=excluded.phase2, content=excluded.content, updated_at=now();
insert into public.sources (id,title,official_source,tier,domain,theme,pathways,core_selective,public_url,phase2,content) values ('M36','DoD Space Policy / Space Strategy public materials','Department of War','Tier 2 - Selective / elective source','Space policy','Oversight, acquisition, transition, and strategic ecosystem','Mission Systems','Selective','https://www.gao.gov/products/gao-26-107959',false,'{"brief":{"Source ID":"M36","Brief ID":"AB-M36","Proposed Brief Title":"DoD Space Policy / Space Strategy public materials","Brief Abstract / Teaching Angle":"This Astrum Brief contextualizes the source for mission-critical space education. It identifies why the material matters now, what it teaches about mission systems, and how it can be translated into an exercise, scenario, or research question rather than remaining a passive reading.","Key Learning Payoff":"National-security space policy context.","What Changed / Why Now":"Astrum uses this source not as static reading, but as a current signal about how mission-critical space systems are being designed, governed, or stressed.","Suggested Dash Deliverable":"2-page memo or 6-slide commander brief uploaded in Dash."},"lens":{"Source ID":"M36","Lens ID":"RL-M36","Raven''s Lens Commentary":"The Raven''s Lens uses the source to surface the trust assumptions hiding underneath the official language.","Hidden Assumption":"That the architecture will behave as designed even when the mission is stressed, degraded, or contested.","Likely Failure Point":"A mismatch between stated policy intent and the technical evidence available during real mission stress.","What They Didn''t Say":"How Astrum''s trust-and-assurance method should be applied to this exact mission problem.","Signature Raven Question":"What part of this strategy fails first if the information environment becomes unreliable?"},"questions":{"Source ID":"M36","CQ-1":"What mission problem is this source really trying to solve?","CQ-2":"What conception of advantage, restraint, and escalation does this source assume?","CQ-3":"What evidence would you want before acting on information from this system?","CQ-4":"Where could adversary pressure, ambiguity, or simple failure distort the picture?","CQ-5":"If you had to teach this to a new Astrum student in ten minutes, what would you emphasize?"},"audio":{"Source ID":"M36","Audio ID":"AA-M36","Episode / Briefing Title":"DoD Space Policy / Space Strategy public materials","Est. Duration":"6-8 min","Voice / Tone":"Documentary-intelligence / authoritative / calm","Opening Hook":"Astrum uses this source to turn static reading into a mission briefing about trust, resilience, and decision quality.","Segment 1":"Situation: define the mission context, the document type, and why it exists now.","Segment 2":"Core content: explain the architecture, framework, strategy, or doctrine in plain operational language.","Segment 3":"Astrum translation: identify the cyber, trust, AI, resilience, or command implications and end with a Raven question.","Closing Raven Question":"What part of this strategy fails first if the information environment becomes unreliable?"},"visual":{"Source ID":"M36","Visual ID":"AV-M36","Asset Title":"Astrum Source Explainer","Recommended Format":"1-page visual brief","Key Story the Visual Should Tell":"Source purpose, system map, trust point, and one decision problem","Must-Show Elements":"A flexible format for any source.","Production Notes":"Use Astrum visual language: dark, precise, premium, and mission-focused."},"aegis":{"Source ID":"M36","Linked Inject IDs":"INJ-12","Suggested Assignment IDs":"A39","Suggested Weekly Activity":"Read the source through the Astrum Brief and Raven''s Lens, listen to or review the audio script, study the visual asset concept, then complete the linked mission task or AEGIS scenario response.","Mission Task Prompt":"Translate the source into a concrete mission decision, architecture judgment, or research gap statement.","Dash Deliverable":"2-page memo or 6-slide commander brief uploaded in Dash.","Evaluation Focus":"Systems thinking, mission relevance, trust-and-assurance reasoning, decision communication, and evidence quality."},"research":{"Source ID":"M36","Research Vector":"Research how doctrine and strategic guidance account for trusted data, cyber resilience, and commercial integration in actual decision chains.","Master''s-Level Option":"20-30 page applied research paper or design study linked to a weekly work plan and AEGIS scenario.","PhD / Publication Option":"Publication-oriented manuscript on the unresolved trust, assurance, architecture, or workforce issue surfaced by the source.","Cross-Links / Best-Fit Pathways":"Mission Systems"}}'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do update set title=excluded.title, official_source=excluded.official_source, tier=excluded.tier, domain=excluded.domain, theme=excluded.theme, pathways=excluded.pathways, core_selective=excluded.core_selective, public_url=excluded.public_url, phase2=excluded.phase2, content=excluded.content, updated_at=now();
insert into public.sources (id,title,official_source,tier,domain,theme,pathways,core_selective,public_url,phase2,content) values ('M37','NASA Systems Engineering Handbook','NASA','Tier 1 - Core Astrum Source','Systems engineering','Mission engineering and systems design','Engineering & Technical Standards','Core','https://www.gao.gov/products/gao-22-105075',false,'{"brief":{"Source ID":"M37","Brief ID":"AB-M37","Proposed Brief Title":"Mission Engineering Discipline for High-Consequence Space Systems","Brief Abstract / Teaching Angle":"This brief extracts the engineering logic from the source and connects it to Astrum''s mission-assurance worldview. Students should see how disciplined systems engineering, mission engineering, interface management, and verification planning can reduce ambiguity, limit cascading failure, and create a more trustworthy operational architecture.","Key Learning Payoff":"Lifecycle systems-engineering practices.","What Changed / Why Now":"Astrum uses this source not as static reading, but as a current signal about how mission-critical space systems are being designed, governed, or stressed.","Suggested Dash Deliverable":"Short written analysis with one visual and a reflective diary entry."},"lens":{"Source ID":"M37","Lens ID":"RL-M37","Raven''s Lens Commentary":"The deeper message here is that rigorous engineering is part of mission ethics. Poor systems discipline creates ambiguity, ambiguity creates misjudgment, and misjudgment is unacceptable in high-consequence space environments.","Hidden Assumption":"That the architecture will behave as designed even when the mission is stressed, degraded, or contested.","Likely Failure Point":"A mismatch between stated policy intent and the technical evidence available during real mission stress.","What They Didn''t Say":"How to operationalize these engineering principles under contested, coalition, and rapidly reconfigurable conditions.","Signature Raven Question":"What mission decision becomes dangerous if the assumptions in this source prove false?"},"questions":{"Source ID":"M37","CQ-1":"What mission problem is this source really trying to solve?","CQ-2":"What trust boundary or dependency deserves the most attention?","CQ-3":"What evidence would you want before acting on information from this system?","CQ-4":"Where could adversary pressure, ambiguity, or simple failure distort the picture?","CQ-5":"How would you convert this reading into a commander brief, exercise, or research question?"},"audio":{"Source ID":"M37","Audio ID":"AA-M37","Episode / Briefing Title":"Mission Engineering Discipline for High-Consequence Space Systems","Est. Duration":"7-9 min","Voice / Tone":"Documentary-intelligence / authoritative / calm","Opening Hook":"Astrum uses this source to turn static reading into a mission briefing about trust, resilience, and decision quality.","Segment 1":"Situation: define the mission context, the document type, and why it exists now.","Segment 2":"Core content: explain the architecture, framework, strategy, or doctrine in plain operational language.","Segment 3":"Astrum translation: identify the cyber, trust, AI, resilience, or command implications and end with a Raven question.","Closing Raven Question":"What mission decision becomes dangerous if the assumptions in this source prove false?"},"visual":{"Source ID":"M37","Visual ID":"AV-M37","Asset Title":"Mission Engineering Crosswalk","Recommended Format":"V-model / lifecycle visual","Key Story the Visual Should Tell":"Stakeholders, mission threads, interfaces, verification, operations","Must-Show Elements":"Use this as a design-thinking asset.","Production Notes":"Use Astrum visual language: dark, precise, premium, and mission-focused."},"aegis":{"Source ID":"M37","Linked Inject IDs":"INJ-12","Suggested Assignment IDs":"A04, A33, A40","Suggested Weekly Activity":"Read the source through the Astrum Brief and Raven''s Lens, listen to or review the audio script, study the visual asset concept, then complete the linked mission task or AEGIS scenario response.","Mission Task Prompt":"Convert engineering guidance into a mission thread and verification plan for an Astrum scenario.","Dash Deliverable":"Short written analysis with one visual and a reflective diary entry.","Evaluation Focus":"Systems thinking, mission relevance, trust-and-assurance reasoning, decision communication, and evidence quality."},"research":{"Source ID":"M37","Research Vector":"Develop a mission-engineering method that explicitly incorporates trust, provenance, and evidence retention.","Master''s-Level Option":"20-30 page applied research paper or design study linked to a weekly work plan and AEGIS scenario.","PhD / Publication Option":"Publication-oriented manuscript on the unresolved trust, assurance, architecture, or workforce issue surfaced by the source.","Cross-Links / Best-Fit Pathways":"Engineering & Technical Standards"}}'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do update set title=excluded.title, official_source=excluded.official_source, tier=excluded.tier, domain=excluded.domain, theme=excluded.theme, pathways=excluded.pathways, core_selective=excluded.core_selective, public_url=excluded.public_url, phase2=excluded.phase2, content=excluded.content, updated_at=now();
